From 463e8fe540d2f0f494c0b72932b4706b33b7c2df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Review <review@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:35:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] tu/mesh: Experimental indexed draw for mesh shaders
 without per-primitive outputs

The generated vertex shader runs once per primitive corner, so a vertex
shared by several primitives of a meshlet is shaded once per use. When the
mesh shader has no per-primitive outputs (nothing can differ between the
primitives sharing a vertex), draw the chunk with an indexed draw instead:
the mesh shader epilogue writes (workgroup << vertex_shift) | vertex per
corner into one contiguous 32 bit index array at the start of the record
region, and the vertex shader runs once per distinct index if the hardware
reuses post-transform vertices (not verified on Adreno), otherwise as often
as before but without the index load and the divisions.

- Off by default. TU_MESH_INDEXED=1 enables it; TU_MESH_INDEXED is read once
  per process at pipeline compile time, so disable the shader cache
  (MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true) when switching it. With it enabled each
  mesh shader logs whether it got the indexed path.
- Pipelines with per-primitive outputs (gl_PrimitiveID, gl_Layer, flat
  per-primitive varyings, ...) keep the vertex-pulling path.
- Dead primitives use TU_MESH_DEAD_VERTEX (0xfffffffe, never the restart
  index); the vertex shader maps it to a clipped position.
- The chunk dispatch is followed by the CP read barrier (clean + wait for
  the ME), since the hardware index fetch is not known to read through UCHE.
- Chunk arguments grow to 48 bytes: the fifth dword of
  VkDrawIndexedIndirectCommand.

Not compiled or run. Identifiers taken on trust and to be checked against the
tree: INDEX4_SIZE_32_BIT, cmd->state.index_size, INDIRECT_OP_INDEXED and the
9 dword CP_DRAW_INDIRECT_MULTI / 7 dword CP_DRAW_INDX_OFFSET layouts (the
latter two match Turnip's own indexed draws as of 2020).
